## Code Style
- Use 2 spaces for indentation.
- Use camelCase for variable and function names.
- Use PascalCase for component and class names.
- Use kebab-case for file names.

## review rule

- Always write correct, best practice, DRY, bug-free, fully functional, and working code.
- Prioritize easy-to-read code over performance.
- Use early returns for readability.
- Always use SCSS for styling.
- Always use `<script setup lang="ts">` for Vue components.
- Use descriptive variable and function names. Event handlers should be prefixed with `handle`, e.g., `handleClick`.
- Implement accessibility features (e.g., `tabindex="0"`, `aria-label`, `@click`, `@keydown`). Example:
  ```vue
  <a
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="Open document"
    @click="handleClick"
    @keydown.enter="handleClick"
  >Open</a>
  ```
- Prefer function declarations over arrow function consts for top-level functions.
- Always use `v-tooltip` for tooltips when a tooltip is needed.
- Always review i18n option in page if any thing updated.
- in .vue file always keep in these order script -> template -> style
- Always use the `useVxeTable` composable for all table/grid implementations. Do not use Element Plus or other table components directly; wrap all table logic and configuration in `useVxeTable` for consistency, maintainability, and access to advanced features.
- Make sure all i18n key are collect and exsit, if not update i18n file in /libraries/deployment/src/

- ALways create new git commit after i18n file change
